            MuscleMeds Carnivor is the budget beef choice. It lists about 23 g of protein per scoop with no fat or sugar, comes in dozens of flavors, and costs less than half as much per gram. It is also a hydrolyzed, collagen-rich beef isolate, so the muscle-building caveat applies equally. The trade is a longer label with sucralose and added flavors. If the clean label is not why you are looking at Be Well, Carnivor does the same job for far less money.
          </p>

          <p>
            Transparent Labs' grass-fed beef isolate is the better-documented alternative, at about 25 g of protein per scoop with stevia, and the brand says it is third-party tested for heavy metals and contaminants. It is a good choice if published testing matters more to you than monk fruit; see our <a href="/transparent-labs-protein-powder-review/">Transparent Labs review</a>. For egg-based dairy-free protein, our <a href="/best-egg-white-protein-powder/">egg white protein guide</a> covers a cheaper option with a more muscle-friendly amino acid profile.
