            Be Well by Kelly makes the cleanest beef protein label we have read: one ingredient in Unflavored, three in Vanilla, Chocolate and Chai, monk fruit as the only sweetener, and 23 to 24 g of protein in about 100 calories per scoop. It is also expensive, at about $2.35 per 25 g, collagen-heavy by the brand's own account, and backed by no testing results we could find.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Buy Vanilla if you need dairy-free animal protein, avoid stevia and sucralose, and own a good blender. If you mainly want dairy-free protein grams, Carnivor gives you the same 23 g for less than half the price, and if you tolerate dairy, a whey isolate is the better muscle-building buy.
          </p>
